From: David Heidelberg <david@ixit.cz>
Subject: [PATCH RESEND v9 9/9] media: qcom: camss: Enable C-PHY where available

After all the changes done we can now safely enable C-PHY for a SoC
where it's available.

Acked-by: Cory Keitz <ckeitz@amazon.com>
Reviewed-by: Bryan O'Donoghue <bod@kernel.org>
Reviewed-by: Frank Li <Frank.Li@nxp.com>
Signed-off-by: David Heidelberg <david@ixit.cz>
Link: https://patchwork.linuxtv.org/project/linux-media/patch/20260729-qcom-cphy-v9-9-1f8d9fdab037@ixit.cz/
Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c | 10 +++++-----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
index 7233349..7808593 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
@@ -5087,11 +5087,11 @@ static int camss_parse_endpoint_node(struct device *dev,
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	/*
-	 * Most SoCs support both D-PHY and C-PHY standards, but currently only
-	 * D-PHY is supported in the driver.
-	 */
-	if (vep.bus_type != V4L2_MBUS_CSI2_DPHY) {
+	switch (vep.bus_type) {
+	case V4L2_MBUS_CSI2_CPHY:
+	case V4L2_MBUS_CSI2_DPHY:
+		break;
+	default:
 		dev_err(dev, "Unsupported bus type %d\n", vep.bus_type);
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
